        "original_id": "ed96d907-a41a-53cc-ad5a-05fb7e079b7f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Eleutherococcus, Amaryllis, Chengiopanax sciadophylloides\n- Taxonomy: Araliaceae, Amaryllidinae, Amaryllideae, genera, species\n\nFacts:\n- Eleutherococcus is a genus of 38 species of thorny shrubs and trees in the family Araliaceae.\n- Amaryllis is the only genus in the subtribe Amaryllidinae of the tribe Amaryllideae.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides was previously included in the genus Eleutherococcus.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides is distinguished from Eleutherococcus by lacking spines or prickles.\n- ITS sequence data confirmed the separation of Chengiopanax sciadophylloides from Eleutherococcus.",
